* Task 7 (FR-20): Adabas record-form UPDATE/DELETE statements
* Record UPDATE and DELETE have no file operand (update the record from preceding READ/FIND/GET)
* UPDATE (label) / DELETE (label) are valid record forms with labels
* SQL UPDATE/DELETE with table identifier + SET/WHERE/FROM remain distinct SQL forms

DEFINE DATA LOCAL
  1 #KEY (N5)
  1 #VAL (A10)
END-DEFINE

READ EMPLOYEES
  * Bare record UPDATE (no label, no operand)
  UPDATE

  * Record UPDATE with label
  UPDATE (0250)

  * Bare record DELETE (no label, no operand)
  DELETE

  * Record DELETE with label
  DELETE (RD.)
END

* SQL UPDATE with table and SET clause (should still parse as SQLUpdateStatement, not record update)
UPDATE MYTABLE SET COL = :#VAL WHERE KEY = :#KEY

* SQL DELETE with FROM clause (should still parse as SQLDeleteStatement, not record delete)
DELETE FROM MYTABLE WHERE KEY = :#KEY

END
